# patches_lossless_savings_calibrate_all_lossless_trial_2026-05-17.tsv

## Provenance
- RFC#45 lossless chunk 5 — lossless-shape trial encoder follow-on to W11-1 (ad9964a6).
- Calibrated against the new trial_encode_ref_frame_bytes_lossless() helper that
  mirrors the live encode_reference_frame_rgb() emit path (XYB-shape trial used
  by W11-1 overshoots true cost by up to 1.8x on smooth-dark UI screenshots).

## Generation
```
cd jxl-encoder--lossless-patches-chunk5
cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder \
  --example patches_lossless_calibrate_all \
  --features __internals \
  2>&1 | grep -E '^(class|screenshot|photo)' \
  > benchmarks/patches_lossless_savings_calibrate_all_lossless_trial_2026-05-17.tsv
```

## Provenance
- Parent commit (main@origin): ddc02a0212fd1d8ac4094184f79f4203fdcbf3a7
- Hostname: lilith
- Date: 2026-05-17 (UTC)
- jxl-encoder version: 0.3.2

## Grid
- 11 gb82-sc screenshots + 5 CID22-512 photos = 16 rows
- LosslessConfig::new() default profile (effort 7)
- patches=true (with the new chunk-5 gate, C=0.35)
- patches=false sidecar for `bytes_off` baseline
- find_and_build_patches_lossless() called directly (no gate) for telemetry

## Schema
class                       screenshot|photo
image                       file basename
width / height              pixels
bytes_off                   bytes with patches disabled
bytes_on                    bytes with patches=default (chunk-5 gate active)
actual_savings_B            bytes_off - bytes_on (signed)
total_patch_pixels          sum over occurrences of ref.xsize * ref.ysize
unique_refs                 PatchesData::ref_positions.len()
ref_frame_pixels            ref_width * ref_height
occurrences                 PatchesData::positions.len()
ref_overhead_xyb_B          trial_encode_ref_frame_bytes (XYB-shape, W11-1 estimator)
ref_overhead_lossless_B     trial_encode_ref_frame_bytes_lossless (chunk-5 estimator)
dict_overhead_B             trial_encode_dict_section_bytes
total_overhead_xyb_B        ref_overhead_xyb_B + dict_overhead_B
total_overhead_lossless_B   ref_overhead_lossless_B + dict_overhead_B
empirical_bpp               actual_savings_B / total_patch_pixels
c_needed_xyb                1.5 * total_overhead_xyb_B / total_patch_pixels
c_needed_lossless           1.5 * total_overhead_lossless_B / total_patch_pixels
overhead_overshoot_ratio    ref_overhead_xyb_B / ref_overhead_lossless_B

## Fit summary
- 8 of 11 screenshots produce PatchesData (3 hit detector's 1% coverage filter)
- 5 of 5 photos return None (no text-like patches)
- bpp distribution over 8 admitted: min=0.048, geomean=0.275, median=0.272,
  mean=0.498, max=2.317
- c_needed_lossless distribution: min=0.183, max=0.350 → C=0.35 admits 8/8
- c_needed_xyb distribution: min=0.186, max=0.437 → W11-1's C=0.45 admitted 8/8
- 22% tighter gate via chunk-5 lossless-shape trial encoder
- 7/8 overhead-overshoot-ratio within +/- 5% (essentially parity); 3 imac entries
  show 1.80x overshoot (smooth-dark UI compresses much better in lossless RGB+RCT
  than in XYB Y/X/B-Y reordered + DC-quant-scaled modular stream)

